    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the elite 82.21 projected efficiency for **Yordan Alvarez**. Facing a favorable matchup against Martinez, his elite 0.477 xwOBA and platoon advantage make him the cornerstone of our lineup. Equally compelling is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), whose speed-first profile is maximized today; facing the slower delivery of Pallante combined with his leadoff spot and a strong platoon edge gives him massive upside in the scarce SB category. **Christian Yelich** also earns a high-confidence start (75.84) at the top of the order, leveraging a strong dynamic platoon edge against Cabrera to keep our early-game pressure high.\n\nOur most significant tactical deployment is **Casey Schmitt** (63.92), who saw his projection skyrocket due to a favorable park factor and a high-leverage SP matchup against Feltner. Conversely, the most difficult personnel decision involved **Luke Raley**, who fell just short of our 40.0 floor at 39.35. While his platoon splits are usually an asset, the matchup against the elite stuff of Cease\u2014who boasts a 3.01 xERA\u2014suppressed his ceiling enough to keep him on the bench. We remain cautious with **Kazuma Okamoto** (52.53) and **Caleb Durbin** (47.16); while both are cleared to start, their matchups against Castillo and Detmers respectively are the most demanding on our board, and we will be monitoring the game flow closely to manage our remaining caps. Note that **Trea Turner** is unavailable due to an off-day, and we continue to track **Rece Hinds** as he remains down with the Jacksonville Jumbo Shrimp.",
